IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `law-licensing`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- ===========================================================================
-- law-duties.l4 — sections 16 and 17 of the Law (Part C: duties of a licence
-- holder). Hebrew copied from law.wiki, compared by eye with Sefer HaChukim
-- 3349, pp. 184-185.
--
-- THE UNIT OF EVERY `WITHIN` IN THIS FILE IS DAYS. `WITHIN` takes a bare
-- number; only this comment and the BECAUSE strings say so (phrasebook 4.3).
--
-- Periods counted forward are counted by Interpretation Law s 10, through the
-- vendored il-interpretation-time.l4, with days of rest, recess or holiday as
-- an input (a function from DATE to BOOLEAN) wherever s 10(c) is applied.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Part C of the Law — duties of a licence holder`

§§ `Section 16 — the duty to update particulars`

-- 16. בעל רישיון יודיע לרשם על כל שינוי בפרטים שמסר בבקשה לרישיון, באופן שעליו
--     יורה הרשם, בתוך 30 ימים מיום השינוי.
--
-- "בתוך 30 ימים מיום השינוי" is a period of days from a day: Interpretation Law
-- s 10(a) does not count the day of the change, so the thirtieth day after it
-- is the last day, inside the period (fork F19, now read from the statute).
-- s 10(c) applies, a deadline for doing something (fork F31): if that day is a
-- day of rest, recess or holiday, the period ends on the first day after it
-- that is not. A notice on the day of the change itself is in time: it is
-- before the deadline. (That is why the module's "inside the period" test,
-- whose period begins the day AFTER the change, is not used here; a notice
-- dated before the change is not a notice of it, and is not in time.)
-- "באופן שעליו יורה הרשם" (in the manner the Registrar
-- directs) is a form requirement with no content in the sources; a notice is
-- taken to be in that manner.
@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN c    IS A `Change of particulars`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` c `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (c's `the day of the change`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law ss 8, 10(a), 10(c)
GIVEN c    IS A `Change of particulars`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 16 — the Registrar was notified in time of` c `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the day the Registrar was notified`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
            d AT LEAST c's `the day of the change`
        AND `s 8 — the date` d `is up to and including` (`section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` c `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest)

-- The duty, on a timeline whose day 0 is the day of the change: WITHIN is the
-- number of days from it to the last day s 10 gives (30, or more where s 10(c)
-- moves the last day). WITHIN is inclusive, so the last day itself is in time.
@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN c    IS A `Change of particulars`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`section 16 — the licence holder shall notify the Registrar of` c `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    PARTY  `the licence holder`
    MUST   `notify the Registrar of the change in particulars`
    WITHIN Day (`section 16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of` c `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest) MINUS Day (c's `the day of the change`)
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the licence holder`
           BECAUSE "s 16: the Registrar was not notified within 30 days of the change in particulars (Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c))"

§§ `Section 17 — the duty to take part in continuing training`

-- 17.(א) בעל רישיון ישתתף במהלך השנה האחרונה לתוקפו של הרישיון, בהשתלמויות בפיקוח
--        המשרד, שערך הרשם או שהאגף להכשרה מקצועית הכיר בהן, בהיקף של שמונה שעות
--        לפחות, בתחום עיסוקו לפי רישיונו, במועדים שעליהם הורה הרשם, ויעמוד בדרישות
--        אותן השתלמויות.
--
-- "the last year of the licence's validity" is the year ending with the last
-- day of the validity period (s. 8): it starts the day after the same date
-- one year earlier. That window is counted BACKWARDS from the end of validity,
-- which Interpretation Law s 10 does not speak of (fork F33), so it is left as
-- it was; its end, the last day of validity, is s 8's and is counted by s 10.
-- A course counts only if every condition the sentence puts on it holds;
-- "בהיקף של שמונה שעות לפחות" is the sum of the counted hours.
@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE, c IS A `Course attended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(a) — the course counts, for a licence whose validity ends on` `the last day of validity` c MEANS
        c's `the day attended` GREATER THAN `add years` `the last day of validity` (0 MINUS 1)
    AND c's `the day attended` AT MOST `the last day of validity`
    AND c's `under the supervision of the Ministry`
    AND c's `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division`
    AND c's `in the field of the holder's work under the licence`
    AND c's `on a date the Registrar directed`
    AND c's `the holder met the course's requirements`

@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE, courses IS A LIST OF `Course attended`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 17(a) — the hours that count, for a licence whose validity ends on` `the last day of validity` courses MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `hours`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `section 17(a) — the course counts, for a licence whose validity ends on` `the last day of validity` c) courses))

@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE, courses IS A LIST OF `Course attended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(a) — the duty is met, for a licence whose validity ends on` `the last day of validity` courses MEANS
    `section 17(a) — the hours that count, for a licence whose validity ends on` `the last day of validity` courses AT LEAST 8

-- The duty as a deontic, on a timeline whose day 0 is the first day of the
-- last year of validity; it runs for as many days as that year has.
@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 17(a) — the number of days in the last year of validity ending on` `the last day of validity` MEANS
    Day `the last day of validity` MINUS Day (`add years` `the last day of validity` (0 MINUS 1))

@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`section 17(a) — the licence holder shall take part in continuing training` `the last day of validity` MEANS
    PARTY  `the licence holder`
    MUST   `take part in at least eight hours of continuing-training courses`
    WITHIN `section 17(a) — the number of days in the last year of validity ending on` `the last day of validity`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the licence holder`
           BECAUSE "s 17(a): fewer than eight hours of qualifying courses in the last year of the licence's validity"

-- (ב) נוסף על ההשתלמויות לפי סעיף קטן (א), הרשם רשאי לדרוש מבעל רישיון להשתתף
--     בהשתלמות מסוימת שערך הרשם או שהאגף להכשרה מקצועית הכיר בה לאחר התייעצות
--     עם המועצה, אם מצא כי מתקיימות נסיבות המצדיקות זאת וכי ההשתתפות נדרשת לשם
--     הכשרת בעל הרישיון ולשם מימוש מטרות חוק זה; הודעה לפי סעיף קטן זה תינתן לבעל
--     הרישיון זמן סביר לפני מועד ההשתלמות.
-- "אם מצא" — if the Registrar found: recorded findings, never computed
-- (phrasebook 8.2). "זמן סביר" is an open standard: an input.
@ref Law s 17(b)
GIVEN `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division after consulting the Council` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar found circumstances that justify it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar found the course needed for the holder's training and for the purposes of this Law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice was given a reasonable time before the course` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(b) — the Registrar may require the holder to take part in this course` MEANS
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division after consulting the Council`
    AND `the Registrar found circumstances that justify it`
    AND `the Registrar found the course needed for the holder's training and for the purposes of this Law`
    AND `notice was given a reasonable time before the course`

-- (ג) הרשם רשאי, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, להאריך את תקופת תוקף רישיונו של בעל רישיון
--     שלא מילא את חובתו להשתתף בהשתלמות לפי סעיף קטן (א) או (ב), במקרים מיוחדים
--     ובנסיבות מוצדקות, בתקופה שלא תעלה על שלושה חודשים, לשם מילוי החובה.
-- "בתקופה שלא תעלה על שלושה חודשים": a period of months after an event, the
-- end of validity. Interpretation Law s 10(b) ends three months after it on
-- the day whose number is that day's (the last day of the month if the month
-- lacks it), inside the period. s 10(c) applies: the extension is a period for
-- doing something, "לשם מילוי החובה" (fork F31), so a last day that is a day of
-- rest, recess or holiday runs on to the first day that is not.
@ref Law s 17(c); Interpretation Law ss 8, 10(b), 10(c)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE,
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE,
      `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(c) — the extension is within the Registrar's power` MEANS
        `the holder did not meet the duty under (a) or (b)`
    AND `the Registrar consulted the Council`
    AND `the Registrar found a special case and justified circumstances`
    AND `the extended last day` GREATER THAN `the last day of validity`
    AND `s 8 — the date` `the extended last day` `is up to and including` (`s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` `the last day of validity` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `days of rest, recess or holiday`)

-- (ד) יראו חובת השתתפות בהשתלמות ועמידה בדרישותיה לפי סעיף זה כתנאי ברישיון של בעל
--     הרישיון.
-- A deeming (phrasebook 7.1). It reaches s. 3(a)'s "ובהתאם לתנאי רישיונו" and
-- s. 10(a)(3) (outside this encoding's scope), both of which this encoding
-- takes as a recorded fact rather than computing from s. 17.
@ref Law s 17(d)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17(d) — taking part in the courses and meeting their requirements is deemed a condition of the licence` MEANS
    TRUE

-- (ה) הרשם יוודא את קיומן, לרבות באמצעות אחר, של השתלמויות, ואת זמינותן.
-- (ו) הרשם יפרסם השתלמויות שהוא עורך והשתלמויות שהאגף להכשרה מקצועית הכיר בהן לפי
--     סעיף זה, באתר האינטרנט של המשרד, זמן סביר לפני מועד ההשתלמות.
-- Duties with no number of days, so no WITHIN (phrasebook 5.9); "זמן סביר"
-- is not a number this encoding can supply.
@ref Law s 17(e)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`section 17(e) — the Registrar shall ensure that courses exist and are available` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST  `ensure that courses exist and are available`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Law s 17(f)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`section 17(f) — the Registrar shall publish the courses` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST  `publish the courses on the Ministry's website`
    HENCE FULFILLED
